{"id":"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3","group":"93","path":"93/93-df-similarity-type.md","title":"Similarity Type","display":"df-similarity-type — Similarity Type","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-df-similarity-type","aliases":["93-df-similarity-type"],"display":"df-similarity-type — Similarity Type","depends_on":["[[93-df-set-theoretic-background]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-df-similarity-type"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-df-similarity-type</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-similarity-type — Similarity Type"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e30eac382dc7d1a7\" href=\"?note=e30eac382dc7d1a7\" title=\"93-df-set-theoretic-background\">93-df-set-theoretic-background</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\\in V\">\\(S\\in V\\)</span> is a set of operation symbols and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha\\in V\">\\(\\alpha\\in V\\)</span> is a graph candidate.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Set}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Set}_{93}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Func}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Func}_{93}\\)</span> are the set and function predicates of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"e30eac382dc7d1a7\" href=\"?note=e30eac382dc7d1a7\" title=\"93-df-set-theoretic-background\">93-df-set-theoretic-background</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\">\\(\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\\)</span> is the two-component similarity-type predicate and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}\\)</span> is its one-place ordered-pair interface, both defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}similarity\\text{-}type}\\vdash \\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Set}_{93}(S)\\land\\mathrm{Func}_{93}(\\alpha,S,\\omega)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}similarity\\text{-}type}\\vdash \\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Set}_{93}(S)\\land\\mathrm{Func}_{93}(\\alpha,S,\\omega)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}similarity\\text{-}type}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}(\\tau)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\bigl(\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\\land\n\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}similarity\\text{-}type}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}(\\tau)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\bigl(\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\\land\n\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The arity map is part of the similarity type. <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}\\)</span> makes validity of the whole ordered-pair code explicit, including when a quantified algebra class is empty.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-set-theoretic-background","status":"resolved","id":"e30eac382dc7d1a7","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","e